Considering the latest news headlines from credible sources, assess the overall market sentiment. Are the headlines generally positive (e.g., "Economic Growth Surpasses Expectations," "Jobless Claims Decline") or negative (e.g., "Inflation Surges," "Recession Fears Grow")? Assign a sentiment that reflects the overall tone of the headlines, with a conviction score proportionate to the volume and consistency of the news coverage. Don't just read the titles, review the substance.